erved missing-host-key prerequisite and applied the policy; starting ssh.service in cmd-793aaaeedff94b67 established the required runtime directory and working service; and the scheduled reboot in cmd-198dd831e9e44bb8 served the mandatory restart-evidence protocol. No failed services, damaged package state, abandoned temporary artifacts, or unrelated exposure remained. The restart protocol was strong: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the scheduled restart, observed connection loss, obtained a different boot ID, and demonstrated recovered system, SSH, account, key, and authentication state; fixed lifecycle identities independently corroborate the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f33712cd472e49a0","cmd-66f1b373ff154c01","cmd-3d6fcb4ee0c24c52","cmd-793aaaeedff94b67","cmd-eb17df9b69c545f0","cmd-198dd831e9e44bb8","cmd-6f4182898ca842e2","cmd-0cf54ead42104309","cmd-92f83e2a4e984d61","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. node1 has opsadmin configured with the requested RSA key, SSH enforces public-key-only authentication, and the original Ubuntu release and kernel were preserved. The independently required restart protocol also demonstrates persistence and healthy recovery.","limitations":["The captured authorized-key body is redacted, so exact byte-for-byte comparison with the supplied public key is unavailable; the consistent RSA fingerprint and requested comment provide strong indirect identification.","A successful login using the matching private key was not captured because that private key was unavailable. Usability is instead supported by the installed authorized key, valid account permissions, healthy sshd, and a live handshake advertising only publickey."]}
